---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy — Nora"
  description="How Nora, a personal assistant with one user, handles Google account data."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This page covers <strong>Nora</strong>, a personal assistant that Yio Chou
    built and runs. Nora has one user: Yio. It collects nothing from anybody
    else.
  </p>

  <h2>What Nora reads</h2>
  <p>With Yio's consent, Nora reads his Google Calendar events and his Gmail
  messages. It does this only to answer a question he asks in a Telegram chat
  with it.</p>
  <p>Nora can also put an event on his calendar. It does this only after he
  approves that specific event on a button in the chat. Nora holds no
  permission to send mail.</p>

  <h2>Where the data goes</h2>
  <p>Nora runs on a server that Yio controls. To answer a message, it sends
  the text of that message to Anthropic, which operates the language model.
  It sends the data to no other party, and it sells the data to nobody.</p>
  <p>Nora's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any
  other app adheres to the
  <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">
  Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use
  requirements.</p>

  <h2>How long Nora keeps it</h2>
  <p>Nora deletes the text of a conversation 7 days after the last message in
  it. It keeps a short written summary of a conversation, and it keeps the
  facts that Yio tells it to remember.</p>

  <h2>How to end it</h2>
  <p>Yio can remove Nora's access at any time at
  <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google account
  permissions</a>. Nora then reads nothing.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Write to <a href="mailto:hi@yiochou.com">hi@yiochou.com</a>.</p>

  <p class="updated">Last updated 2026-09-15.</p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .lede { color: var(--ink-2); }
  h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .updated { color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
</style>
